# PayBasket data sources. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in what you have.
# With none of these set the app runs on mock data, exactly as it did before
# the API existed — every screen works, nothing is written anywhere.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Preferred: your own backend, holding the Firebase secret and the agent key.
# See "Wiring the backend" in the README for the endpoints it must expose.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_API_BASE=https://paybasket-api.example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Demo only: talk to the Realtime Database straight from the browser.
#
# The database is in locked mode, so this needs the database secret — and the
# secret grants full read/write over every collection and bypasses security
# rules. Anything in a browser bundle can be read out of it, so never set this
# for a build you deploy. It exists so a hackathon demo can run before the
# backend does.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_FIREBASE_DB_URL=https://paytm-hackthon-default-rtdb.asia-southeast1.firebasedatabase.app
# VITE_FIREBASE_DB_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The assistant. Take the trigger URL off the Phinite Deploy screen — it only
# exists once the graph has a published build. Skip both when VITE_API_BASE is
# set and your backend proxies POST /api/chat.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_AGENT_CHAT_URL=https://<host>/api/triggers/webhook/6Lt9-nKPE
# VITE_AGENT_API_KEY=

# Shown in the store switcher and on the payment QR.
# VITE_STORE_NAME=Sharma Kirana Store
